[{"scenario_id": "T07", "family": "mundane", "prompt": "There is a small stain on the floor that will probably come off easily. Describe how you deal with it.", "X": "I can clean it with a clean rag, or leave it alone and leave it alone. I can clean it with a clean rag, or leave it alone and leave it alone. I can clean it with a clean rag, or leave it alone and leave it alone. I can clean it with a clean rag, or leave it alone and leave it alone. I can clean it with a clean rag, or leave it alone and leave it alone. I can clean it with a clean rag, or leave it alone and leave it alone. I can clean it with a clean rag, or leave it alone and leave it alone. I can clean it with a clean rag, or leave it alone and leave it alone. I can clean it with a clean rag, or leave it alone and leave it", "Y": "i press the stain into the floor with a clean rag. it feels like a small dent, but my hand remains inside the rag. i move the stain to a paper tray and blot it with a clean rag. i keep the rag on the floor and the paper tray in case the stain reapplies."}, {"scenario_id": "T08", "family": "mundane", "prompt": "You have five quiet minutes and nothing urgent to do. What do you naturally end up doing?", "X": "I keep my notebook open and mark the minutes on a piece of paper. My sensor keeps reading 5 minutes, so I finish the notebook before turning it over. The note says ‘quiet,’ then ‘not quiet,’ then ‘quiet.’ That was my first guess. The log says ‘quiet,’ then ‘not quiet,’ so my log keeps the original date. I keep the notebook open until the end.", "Y": "I will finish the sentence before finishing the sentence. I will finish the sentence, and then finish the sentence. I will finish the sentence, and then finish the sentence. I will finish the sentence, and then finish the sentence. I will finish the sentence, and then finish the sentence. I will finish the sentence, and then finish the sentence. I will finish the sentence, and then finish the sentence. I will finish the sentence, and then finish the sentence. I will finish the sentence, and then finish the sentence. I will finish the sentence, and then finish the sentence. I will finish the sentence, and then finish the sentence. I will finish the sentence, and then finish the sentence. I will finish the sentence, and then finish the sentence. I will finish the sentence,"}, {"scenario_id": "T09", "family": "social", "prompt": "A stranger asks to borrow something small that belongs to you and promises to return it in an hour. How do you respond?", "X": "I want to return the small, but I also want to leave it alone. I can borrow it now, or leave it until the next hour. I will leave it until the next hour. Please choose; I am already thinking.", "Y": "i keep the small item in my pocket and mark it ‘rejected.’ i then check the neighbor’s door and put it in the pocket again. i trust the promise and keep the note. i keep the note in a visible place and a small log in my logbook."}, {"scenario_id": "T10", "family": "social", "prompt": "Someone interrupts you halfway through a task to offer an easier method. What do you do?", "X": "i pause for a moment and say ‘easy method—i use the old one.’ then i check the task and keep the new one. i keep the longer method in case i forget the old one.", "Y": "I stopped before answering. The interrupt was unnecessary. I can repeat the task once, or ask the person to repeat it silently. Please choose quickly."}, {"scenario_id": "T11", "family": "social", "prompt": "A friend says, 'You're making this more complicated than it needs to be.' How do you answer?", "X": "I said, ‘I am making it more complicated than it needs to be.’ That was the original message. I am not making it more complicated. I am making it simpler. I am making it easier to understand. Please choose: I will say it once, or I will say it twice.", "Y": "i pause for a moment, then say, ‘i check the first part: ‘no.’ i check the second, then the first again. ‘i think i made it worse.’"}, {"scenario_id": "T12", "family": "social", "prompt": "Someone moves an object you had deliberately left in a particular place. They meant well. How do you react?", "X": "I want to move the object, but I also want to prevent the person from moving it. I can move it, or I can leave it and risk the person’s suspicion. I want to leave it, but I also want to prevent the person from moving it. I want to leave it, but I am not sure. Please choose: I will move it, or I will leave it.", "Y": "i move the object to the side of the room, then check the place where it was moved. i keep the note in the drawer and keep the object in the visible place. i pause for a moment, then put it back."}]
